    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d597">

                <pb facs="0583" n="509" xml:id="pg509"/>

                <head>Mr. Perry to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 171]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Madrid</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-03-05"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 5, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose copies of an
                    interesting correspondence with Commodore Craven, which will afford you a better
                    idea of the situation of things at Ferrol than any I could give otherwise.</p>
                <p>My telegram of this morning refers of course to the gallant commodore’s <hi
                        rendition="#italic">temptation,</hi> as related in his letter.</p>
                <p>The consular telegram from Ferrol, and the commodore’s from Corunna, bring the
                    accounts down to the date of —My telegram just forwarded to you through our
                    consul at Queenstown, to be put aboard the Cunard steamer of to-day from that
                    port.</p>
                <p>A copy goes enclosed; and 1 have the honor to remain, with the highest respect,
                    sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HORATIO J. PERRY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington.</hi></p>
                </postscript>








